# Load-bearing in two ways, not one. The rollback button has always run
# /usr/libexec/phoenix-restore. Since Stage U, /usr/lib/shadowfetch/sfupdate
# also IMPORTS phoenix.trusted: the executable-trust classifier is shared
# rather than duplicated, because two implementations of "can somebody other
# than root substitute this binary" is the defect, not the fix. Demoting this
# to Recommends breaks fireproofd at import.
 shadowfetch-phoenix
Recommends:
 snapper,
 libnotify-bin
# This package writes sfcc/fireproof_page.py into the Python package that
# shadowfetch-control-center owns, and the Control Center imports it by name
# from software_page.py. Until this line, neither debian/control mentioned the
# other: a cross-package module drop with no declared relationship in either
# direction, which is exactly the edge a partial install breaks and a full ISO
# hides. Enhances is the accurate relation -- Fireproof is complete on its own
# (fireproof(1), fireproofd, the apt hooks), and the page is an addition to
# another package -- so it declares the seam without dragging PyQt6 and the
# whole desktop onto a headless install.
Enhances: shadowfetch-control-center
Description: Shadowfetch Fireproof safe system updates
 Fireproof is how Shadowfetch Linux updates itself. Opening the analyze
 screen takes no apt lock and downloads nothing: the pending upgrade is
 simulated read-only (python3-apt, same resolver as apt), holds surface
 as pinned, library renames collapse to one line, and critical packages
 are flagged red. The dpkg lock is taken only at commit, where the
 approved change-set hash is re-validated first.
 .
 Updates are wrapped in a Phoenix Point automatically by snapper's own
 apt hooks - Fireproof creates zero snapshots of its own, it only names
 the first pre-snapshot of the transaction as the rollback target. After
 the commit a headless verify battery checks dpkg consistency, initrd
 freshness, GRUB, dkms modules, newly failed services, and the network;
 if the desktop ever fails to come back, the next boot opens recovery at
 exactly the right Point. One command (fireproof) drives everything the
 page can do. No telemetry, no unattended downloads or installs.
